# Normalize line endings to LF in the repository AND in the working tree.
#
# Not just tidiness. The Dockerfile is consumed by Docker on Linux, and a CRLF
# line ending turns the HEALTHCHECK's exec-form JSON into
#   ["node", "-e", "...\r"]
# where the carriage return becomes part of the argument. Git for Windows
# defaults to core.autocrlf=true, so without this rule a Windows checkout is
# not byte-identical to what the container expects.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Never touch binaries.
*.node binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.gz binary
*.tgz binary
